WEBVTT

00:00.990 --> 00:01.980
Teika...

00:02.520 --> 00:04.570
Sing for me, Teika...

00:10.710 --> 00:12.360
Teika-dono!

00:12.360 --> 00:14.190
Have you gone out?

00:15.020 --> 00:16.880
Oh, you're here.

00:17.520 --> 00:19.800
You weren't responding.

00:19.800 --> 00:21.270
Were you taking a nap?

00:23.080 --> 00:24.840
I was dreaming...

00:25.890 --> 00:27.540
About the past...

02:07.060 --> 02:08.530
Kemari?

02:07.060 --> 02:08.530
Oh, sorry.

02:08.530 --> 02:10.490
That won't do.

02:10.490 --> 02:13.140
You can't fight the world like that.

02:13.140 --> 02:15.820
What are you talking about?

02:16.220 --> 02:20.900
And why is the son of Fujiwara
no Shunzei, a prominent poet,

02:20.900 --> 02:23.510
good at kemari, Teika?

02:23.510 --> 02:27.030
Please, don't try to stereotype me.

02:27.030 --> 02:29.960
I'm my own man.
I'm not a clone of Shunzei!

02:30.370 --> 02:32.270
Ooh, that sounds cool.

02:31.320 --> 02:33.420
I'll let him be for now.

02:33.710 --> 02:35.220
Here I go!

02:33.710 --> 02:35.800
I was also young once.

02:36.090 --> 02:37.130
Oh, stupid!

02:38.850 --> 02:41.590
Right, I'm still young!

02:42.320 --> 02:44.810
I can do anything!

02:49.770 --> 02:52.770
Teika and Noriko

02:49.770 --> 02:52.770
Princess Shokushi
Gon Chunagon Teika

02:53.190 --> 02:55.730
Teika, you are 19.

02:55.730 --> 02:58.740
You should try to settle down.

02:58.740 --> 03:00.500
I'm getting old...

03:02.090 --> 03:04.780
F-For example, you could study poetry?

03:04.780 --> 03:06.150
Just to be clear,

03:06.150 --> 03:08.940
I have no intention of
following in your footsteps.

03:08.940 --> 03:09.910
Wh-What?!

03:10.370 --> 03:13.580
I didn't choose to be
born in this family.

03:13.580 --> 03:14.720
W-Wait.

03:14.720 --> 03:16.380
You have tremendous poetic talent.

03:16.840 --> 03:18.990
For your own good, I'm telling you to—

03:18.990 --> 03:20.760
That's what I can't stand!

03:21.460 --> 03:26.560
You try to dictate my life while
saying that it's "for your own good."

03:26.560 --> 03:28.680
A child isn't supposed to be
their parents' plaything!

03:29.010 --> 03:31.770
I'm never going to become a poet!

03:33.540 --> 03:38.960
Very well, I must go instruct
Her Highness in poetry.

03:38.960 --> 03:41.610
We will continue this
conversation afterwards.

03:44.180 --> 03:47.810
Honestly, he sounds like
a boy in middle school.

03:48.670 --> 03:53.170
However, his talent is undeniable.

03:53.660 --> 03:56.410
I cannot allow it to waste away.

03:58.540 --> 04:02.200
Isn't there a button I can
press to motivate him?

04:05.390 --> 04:07.220
I can't believe he's telling
me to settle down.

04:11.410 --> 04:13.330
Is Shunzei-dono around?

04:13.330 --> 04:15.830
Oh, he just went out.

04:16.260 --> 04:17.360
Uh...

04:17.360 --> 04:18.430
Who are you?

04:18.430 --> 04:20.690
Oh, excuse me.

04:21.540 --> 04:23.360
My name is Saigyo.

04:28.060 --> 04:31.160
Yes, Noriko-sama is very bright,

04:31.720 --> 04:33.870
and she's a hard worker,

04:33.870 --> 04:35.560
which makes teaching
her very enjoyable.

04:36.170 --> 04:37.780
Meanwhile...

04:40.350 --> 04:41.230
Teika...

04:41.230 --> 04:42.770
Oh, Father.

04:42.770 --> 04:44.300
You're back?

04:44.300 --> 04:45.780
Y-Yes...

04:45.780 --> 04:47.780
I'm sure it's hard work to travel to

04:47.780 --> 04:50.260
a student's home to teach poetry.

04:50.970 --> 04:52.990
Did something happen?

04:53.420 --> 04:55.250
Oh?  Can you tell?

04:55.250 --> 04:57.060
You can tell?

04:57.640 --> 05:01.770
Actually, I've decided to work
towards becoming a poet.

05:01.770 --> 05:03.780
What?!  I-Is that true?!

05:04.060 --> 05:05.040
Yes.

05:05.040 --> 05:07.830
Oh, you've changed your mind!

05:07.830 --> 05:11.010
You've realized your
responsibilities as my heir!

05:11.920 --> 05:13.750
Oh.  Just to be clear,

05:13.750 --> 05:16.040
I won't be following in your footsteps.

05:17.080 --> 05:19.810
I'm going to grow up to
be like Saigyo-dono.

05:19.810 --> 05:21.570
Sa-Saigyo?

05:21.570 --> 05:23.940
He just dropped by.

05:24.360 --> 05:27.720
It was our first meeting,
but I was deeply impressed.

05:27.720 --> 05:32.840
W-Well, I agree that
he's a talented poet,

05:32.840 --> 05:35.150
but you want to be like him?

05:35.150 --> 05:37.060
I want to be an outlaw poet.

05:38.110 --> 05:39.940
At the young age of 23,

05:39.940 --> 05:42.520
he defied convention and became a monk!

05:42.520 --> 05:44.030
He lives free as the wind,

05:44.030 --> 05:46.190
paying no heed to social
status or personal glory.

05:46.190 --> 05:49.870
He travels as he pleases
and composes poetry.

05:50.580 --> 05:57.260
His solitary sensibility turned
his very way of life into art.

05:57.600 --> 06:00.820
That's the kind of poet I want to be.

06:00.820 --> 06:04.170
Yes, there are people in
the 21st century who talk

06:04.170 --> 06:06.970
about traveling after
graduating from college,

06:06.970 --> 06:08.770
instead of finding a job.

06:08.770 --> 06:09.890
What's this?

06:09.890 --> 06:12.230
Do I hear the jealousy
of a cog in the machine?

06:12.230 --> 06:14.230
Who are you calling a cog?

06:14.230 --> 06:18.190
You realize this cog is why you're
able to sit at home all day.

06:18.740 --> 06:21.640
Well, I won't say that his
way of life is wrong,

06:21.640 --> 06:24.360
as long as you're following some ideal.

06:24.710 --> 06:29.450
But in your case, you're just
posing out of curiosity.

06:29.450 --> 06:31.440
You talk too much!

06:32.170 --> 06:36.560
Anyway, I'm not becoming a
boot-licking poet like you!

06:36.560 --> 06:40.140
I'm becoming a soulful
poet like Saigyo-dono!

06:40.140 --> 06:41.540
Soulful?

06:42.020 --> 06:44.290
Well, you're free to become a poet,

06:44.290 --> 06:47.360
but don't talk about becoming a monk.

06:47.940 --> 06:50.310
Hmm...  become a monk...

06:50.310 --> 06:51.390
That's a wonderful idea.

06:51.390 --> 06:53.930
Foot in Mouth

06:54.350 --> 06:55.640
What?

06:55.640 --> 06:57.690
Teika-kun wishes to become a monk?

06:57.690 --> 06:59.460
That's right, Saigyo!

06:59.460 --> 07:01.730
What did you tell him?

07:02.390 --> 07:04.260
Nothing in particular.

07:04.260 --> 07:06.690
I told him about my travels and poetry.

07:06.690 --> 07:10.400
Honestly, you are a toxic influence.

07:10.400 --> 07:12.990
Do you realize how many
young people have

07:12.990 --> 07:15.410
made poor decisions because of you?

07:16.940 --> 07:20.080
What if he really becomes a monk?

07:21.510 --> 07:23.040
Why don't you get him married?

07:23.470 --> 07:24.820
Married?

07:24.820 --> 07:27.360
Young people do crazy things

07:27.360 --> 07:29.230
because they have nothing to protect.

07:29.230 --> 07:31.510
Once they're married and have children,

07:31.510 --> 07:34.820
it's a much harder decision
to become a monk.

07:35.460 --> 07:37.160
No, your logic is flawed.

07:38.450 --> 07:41.300
You left behind your wife and
children when you became a monk.

07:46.280 --> 07:49.150
That is a very amusing tale.

07:49.540 --> 07:52.250
Please don't laugh, Your Highness.

07:52.250 --> 07:54.300
I am truly at my wit's end.

07:54.790 --> 07:57.120
My son is very stubborn.

07:57.120 --> 08:00.740
At this rate, he may end
up becoming a monk.

08:02.090 --> 08:04.580
If you wouldn't mind, Shunzei-dono...

08:05.440 --> 08:08.440
Could you introduce me to your son?

08:08.440 --> 08:11.290
What?  To Teika?

08:11.290 --> 08:12.050
Yes.

08:12.630 --> 08:15.450
Instead of forcing him into a
confined world and causing him stress,

08:15.450 --> 08:19.350
if you bring him into a new
environment with new poetry,

08:19.350 --> 08:21.560
he may change his mind.

08:23.590 --> 08:27.940
Although, I don't know if
I'll be able to help.

08:27.940 --> 08:30.870
No, I am grateful for your assistance.

08:30.870 --> 08:32.610
Thank you.

08:33.310 --> 08:35.030
Princess Noriko?

08:35.400 --> 08:39.460
Yes, she once served as the
High Priestess of Kamo.

08:39.460 --> 08:42.920
I've been instructing her in poetry.

08:42.920 --> 08:45.980
She wants to meet you.

08:46.800 --> 08:48.780
Something's fishy about this.

08:49.320 --> 08:50.720
Wh-What do you mean?

08:50.720 --> 08:53.690
Why would someone that
important want to meet me?

08:54.910 --> 08:58.040
You must have told her
that I'm your heir!

08:58.040 --> 08:59.750
I don't intend to take over for you!

08:59.750 --> 09:00.650
No, no!

09:00.650 --> 09:02.850
Her Highness is a dedicated student,

09:02.850 --> 09:06.100
and she wishes to meet different poets.

09:06.470 --> 09:10.410
So could you meet with her,
for your father's sake?

09:11.740 --> 09:15.800
If Her Highness wants to
see me, I have to oblige.

09:16.860 --> 09:18.280
Just as planned.

09:18.710 --> 09:22.330
Teika needs a reason to work.

09:22.330 --> 09:26.370
If he knows there is someone
near him worth serving...

09:28.850 --> 09:30.530
I'm nervous...

09:40.800 --> 09:42.380
Nice to meet you.

09:42.380 --> 09:44.220
You must be Teika.

09:47.920 --> 09:49.730
How did it go, Teika?

09:50.450 --> 09:52.100
Why are you in a daze?

09:52.100 --> 09:53.860
Did you do something rude?

09:55.200 --> 09:58.330
Father, I will follow in your footsteps

09:58.330 --> 09:59.820
and become a proper poet.

09:59.820 --> 10:03.540
Court                                     Military

10:00.540 --> 10:02.090
Saigyo-dono is a military noble.

10:02.090 --> 10:03.540
I am a court noble.

10:03.920 --> 10:06.390
As someone born into a noble family,

10:06.390 --> 10:09.270
I wish to expand the
culture within the palace!

10:09.270 --> 10:11.540
Yes!  Beautifully put, Teika!

10:11.950 --> 10:14.840
Father!  From this day forward,

10:14.840 --> 10:16.960
I will call you Teacher!

10:16.960 --> 10:19.130
Yes, I'll do my best!

10:19.500 --> 10:21.440
Her Highness is amazing.

10:21.440 --> 10:24.310
I'm so glad I sent him to her.

10:24.310 --> 10:25.770
By the way, Father.

10:26.610 --> 10:31.160
Have you ever seen Her
Highness' face before?

10:31.160 --> 10:32.550
No, of course not.

10:32.550 --> 10:36.240
I am not worthy enough to see her face.

10:36.240 --> 10:38.180
Of course...

10:38.180 --> 10:40.160
I guess I don't have a chance then...

10:40.160 --> 10:40.920
Hmm?

10:40.920 --> 10:43.130
She was a remarkable person.

10:43.130 --> 10:46.930
The kind of person you
would call a true lady.

10:47.510 --> 10:49.620
And she smelled nice.

10:49.620 --> 10:51.450
Her writing was wonderful,

10:51.450 --> 10:55.380
and I can't get that sweet
voice out of my mind.

10:55.980 --> 10:57.430
T-Teika?

10:57.430 --> 11:00.920
I'm sure you realize that, to men like us,

11:00.920 --> 11:03.090
she is beyond even the clouds.

11:03.690 --> 11:06.600
Oh, right.  I know that.

11:07.300 --> 11:12.560
Still, I'm free to wish upon the
clouds for a chance to fly in the sky.

11:13.410 --> 11:18.030
Have I made a terrible mistake?

11:20.570 --> 11:24.640
You have a wealth of knowledge
and your poetry is eloquent,

11:24.640 --> 11:26.370
but it sounds superficial.

11:28.330 --> 11:31.500
I'm still young, so I don't
have enough experience yet...

11:31.870 --> 11:33.930
What sort of experience do you lack?

11:33.930 --> 11:35.560
Well...

11:35.560 --> 11:37.080
I have no experience in love,

11:37.080 --> 11:39.690
since I never had any opportunity.

11:40.180 --> 11:43.300
In that case, Teika...

11:43.920 --> 11:46.230
Would you care to
experience love with me?

11:48.310 --> 11:50.390
What?!

11:51.500 --> 11:54.400
Love?!  Love?!  Love?!

11:54.400 --> 11:56.730
Experience love with Noriko-sama?!

11:57.230 --> 11:59.330
But of course, it will
only be make-believe.

11:59.230 --> 12:01.440
Make-believe

12:00.360 --> 12:01.450
Make-believe...

12:01.450 --> 12:02.900
Naturally.

12:04.430 --> 12:08.160
I once served the Gods
as High Priestess.

12:08.930 --> 12:11.000
I've never fallen in love,

12:11.660 --> 12:15.000
but if I were to fall in love,

12:15.000 --> 12:17.320
it would cause me much pain.

12:17.320 --> 12:19.630
That is why I compose poems of love.

12:20.790 --> 12:22.430
You see, Teika...

12:22.430 --> 12:25.470
Poetry is a test of your imagination.

12:26.050 --> 12:28.950
You will struggle if you are unable

12:28.950 --> 12:31.120
to compose poetry about that which

12:31.120 --> 12:33.130
you have yet to experience.

12:33.560 --> 12:34.490
So how about it?

12:35.160 --> 12:37.230
Would you like to exchange
love poems with me,

12:37.230 --> 12:39.600
as part of your study?

12:40.590 --> 12:43.070
If you and I fell in love,
it would have to be a secret.

12:43.880 --> 12:46.070
That makes this the perfect assignment.

12:48.330 --> 12:50.640
E-Er, then...

12:50.640 --> 12:55.140
If secret love is like the lily
petal hidden in the grass,

12:55.140 --> 12:58.250
overflowing emotion is like the
firefly which illuminates the night.

12:58.250 --> 13:01.300
My, you're very good.

13:01.700 --> 13:04.470
I will try to match your skill.

13:04.470 --> 13:07.150
Th-Thank you very much...

13:09.380 --> 13:12.240
Some people are able
to hide their love,

13:12.900 --> 13:17.680
but my love is as bright
as the light of a firefly,

13:18.240 --> 13:19.490
so I cannot conceal it.

13:24.050 --> 13:28.030
After following the message
in the cool breeze,

13:28.630 --> 13:31.740
I discovered a flawless
wild lily in the brush.

13:34.080 --> 13:35.540
An adorable person...

13:38.470 --> 13:42.340
As of late, when I gaze
beyond the clouds,

13:42.950 --> 13:45.750
I am reminded of my love for
one who is out of reach.

13:46.500 --> 13:48.890
That's very sweet.

13:48.890 --> 13:49.800
Yes!

13:50.430 --> 13:54.000
That poem was supposed to
reflect our first meeting.

13:55.760 --> 13:58.810
You have a wonderful imagination.

13:59.180 --> 14:01.940
Actually, when I think about you,

14:01.940 --> 14:04.110
these love poems just pop into my head!

14:04.380 --> 14:05.850
Just kidding.

14:06.420 --> 14:10.760
In that case, how would
you respond to this poem?

14:10.760 --> 14:12.580
We're still exchanging poems?

14:16.080 --> 14:17.820
I'm eager to see your response.

14:17.820 --> 14:19.290
Oh, yes...

14:22.420 --> 14:23.980
Teika, I'm coming in.

14:25.280 --> 14:26.720
Oh, he isn't here?

14:28.280 --> 14:30.890
Oh, has he been exchanging poems?

14:32.560 --> 14:35.090
This is a love poem.

14:35.090 --> 14:37.410
It appears that he's been busy.

14:37.900 --> 14:39.230
However...

14:39.940 --> 14:41.230
This handwriting...

14:41.670 --> 14:43.190
and this scent...

14:43.930 --> 14:47.210
Nothing can be worse
than living a moment longer

14:47.210 --> 14:50.590
when I cannot bear growing any weaker

14:50.590 --> 14:52.300
than I already have.

14:54.130 --> 14:58.300
If I must conceal my love until
I can no longer bear it,

14:58.770 --> 15:01.150
I would rather end it all now.

15:02.740 --> 15:06.170
This poem is well-crafted,
but could it be...

15:07.740 --> 15:09.580
What are you doing, Father?!

15:10.840 --> 15:12.300
Honestly!

15:12.560 --> 15:15.130
You shouldn't be digging
through my belongings!

15:15.430 --> 15:16.840
Say, Teika,

15:16.840 --> 15:18.910
about that poem...

15:18.910 --> 15:19.600
What?

15:19.980 --> 15:22.220
Was it composed by...

15:23.870 --> 15:26.360
Oh, it was Noriko-sama.

15:28.330 --> 15:30.170
It's a beautiful poem, right?

15:30.170 --> 15:32.950
I-Indeed, but...

15:33.600 --> 15:36.390
Don't tell me that you've...

15:37.430 --> 15:40.860
made a grave mistake?

15:42.130 --> 15:43.780
What are you talking about?

15:43.780 --> 15:45.250
Uh, well...

15:45.250 --> 15:47.290
No, no, no!  Definitely not!

15:47.290 --> 15:48.650
This is make-believe!

15:48.650 --> 15:50.990
We pretend we're lovers
and write poems!

15:50.990 --> 15:52.280
Haven't you done that before?

15:52.280 --> 15:53.010
Yeah...

15:53.010 --> 15:55.220
Why would you think it was real?!

15:55.220 --> 15:57.600
She's 13 years older than I am,

15:57.600 --> 15:59.720
and she's a princess who
served as High Priestess!

15:59.720 --> 16:01.670
It's completely out of the question!

16:02.380 --> 16:04.270
Yikes, I don't believe it.

16:04.270 --> 16:05.680
The great poet Shunzei harbored

16:05.680 --> 16:07.270
such impure thoughts about poetry!

16:07.660 --> 16:12.010
Sorry about that.
It sounded so real.

16:12.420 --> 16:14.810
So?  Did you need something?

16:14.810 --> 16:15.820
Oh, that's right.

16:16.550 --> 16:18.560
I have a potential bride for you.

16:18.560 --> 16:19.290
Huh?

16:19.690 --> 16:22.150
Rokujo-san's daughter.

16:22.150 --> 16:23.970
Well?  Interested in meeting her?

16:23.970 --> 16:26.190
Oops, I need to get to work.

16:26.190 --> 16:28.710
W-Wait, Teika.
You'd just be talking—

16:28.710 --> 16:29.160
Bye!

16:29.160 --> 16:29.880
Teika!

16:30.490 --> 16:32.690
Damn that senile old man.

16:32.690 --> 16:34.640
What was he calling a mistake?

16:34.640 --> 16:36.480
I'm going to tell Noriko-sama

16:36.480 --> 16:38.680
that my father's lost his mind.

16:38.680 --> 16:40.510
A mistake?

16:40.850 --> 16:42.060
Idiocy...

16:42.060 --> 16:43.740
Pure idiocy!

16:43.740 --> 16:47.110
I'm sorry to say that this
is 100% make-believe!

16:47.720 --> 16:50.240
Yes, this is a game.

16:50.240 --> 16:52.250
Poems about fake love.

16:52.800 --> 16:56.260
I may pour my heart into
the poems I send you,

16:56.260 --> 16:58.650
but you will pay me no heed.

17:00.550 --> 17:02.790
You seem upset, Teika.

17:03.830 --> 17:05.310
Did something happen?

17:06.280 --> 17:10.190
Oh, I got in a fight with
my father as I was leaving.

17:11.240 --> 17:12.940
With Shunzei-dono?

17:12.940 --> 17:14.160
What happened?

17:14.740 --> 17:20.010
Well, he wanted to set
me up with a bride.

17:21.090 --> 17:22.580
A bride...

17:22.580 --> 17:25.590
Honestly, I'm not very interested,

17:25.590 --> 17:28.870
because I already have you!

17:28.870 --> 17:30.520
Just kidding!

17:30.520 --> 17:32.170
Enough joking around.

17:32.820 --> 17:34.990
You should accept the offer.

17:35.640 --> 17:38.200
It would be wrong to make
trouble for Shunzei-dono.

17:40.420 --> 17:41.850
Uh, so...

17:41.850 --> 17:44.290
I was expecting you to
respond with a joke.

17:44.290 --> 17:47.590
A poem about how you would curse me

17:47.590 --> 17:50.320
for leaving you for another woman.

17:50.710 --> 17:52.880
This is an occasion where
we should be serious.

17:53.930 --> 17:56.780
I am learning poetry as a hobby,

17:56.780 --> 17:59.080
but you were born into
a family of poets.

17:59.680 --> 18:02.510
It is your duty to have children
and pass on your family's poems.

18:03.100 --> 18:06.130
I am not sure why you would refuse,

18:06.130 --> 18:08.630
but you must stop acting like a child.

18:09.750 --> 18:10.930
You should marry.

18:11.830 --> 18:14.940
Then I'll give you a serious answer.

18:15.510 --> 18:17.240
I'm in love with you!

18:17.970 --> 18:20.310
That's why I don't want to get married!

18:21.770 --> 18:24.320
Stop joking around...

18:24.320 --> 18:26.080
Which one of us is joking around?!

18:27.230 --> 18:29.610
You're the one who came up

18:29.610 --> 18:32.540
with this game to belittle my emotions!

18:33.480 --> 18:34.620
Teika!

18:34.620 --> 18:36.170
These feelings aren't make-believe!

18:36.480 --> 18:38.630
I truly love you!

18:38.990 --> 18:41.890
How long will this game continue?!

18:42.820 --> 18:45.350
Do not ask me for anything
more than make-believe love!

18:47.570 --> 18:50.060
Let go of me, Teika.

18:50.810 --> 18:52.260
You are making me uncomfortable.

18:55.540 --> 18:56.760
I'm sorry...

18:58.120 --> 18:59.150
I will never return.

19:01.680 --> 19:03.600
Don't say that.

19:04.080 --> 19:05.790
Please visit me again.

19:06.750 --> 19:09.000
We can exchange poems.

19:09.900 --> 19:12.140
You're a cruel person.

19:12.660 --> 19:15.350
How can you ask that of me?!

19:15.350 --> 19:17.600
Yes, I'm a cruel person!

19:18.710 --> 19:23.040
Make-believe love is all I have...

19:24.470 --> 19:25.650
Only poetry...

19:26.200 --> 19:30.170
Only poetry can liberate me
from the prison I live in.

19:31.360 --> 19:33.180
I can do nothing more
than compose poems.

19:34.350 --> 19:37.290
So please, I beg you...

19:38.230 --> 19:40.700
Sing for me, Teika.

19:41.300 --> 19:43.170
Forgive me.

19:45.860 --> 19:48.530
That's cruel.  So cruel...

19:49.260 --> 19:51.320
I've been caught by a cruel woman.

19:56.430 --> 20:00.220
Though my feelings and dreams
will never be realized,

20:00.870 --> 20:02.510
I only ask that you bear growing weaker

20:02.510 --> 20:04.350
than you already have.

20:06.870 --> 20:08.760
I will feel pained as I think of you.

20:09.390 --> 20:11.020
I will feel empty as I long for you,

20:12.340 --> 20:16.400
but please do not let
yourself disappear.

20:18.780 --> 20:21.410
This is my reply to the poem you sent.

20:22.260 --> 20:23.200
Teika...

20:23.590 --> 20:26.410
I will return, Noriko-sama.

20:27.060 --> 20:29.570
We're free to sing of our dreams, yes?

20:30.760 --> 20:33.690
Yes, let us sing together.

20:34.920 --> 20:37.820
Kennin 1

20:34.920 --> 20:37.820
January 25

20:47.350 --> 20:49.640
Princess Shokushi

20:47.350 --> 20:49.640
passes away

20:52.290 --> 20:54.540
Now that Noriko-sama is gone,

20:54.540 --> 20:56.520
my secret love is over.

20:57.500 --> 20:59.580
It would only cause me more pain

20:59.580 --> 21:01.060
to leave the poems we exchanged.

21:01.710 --> 21:04.190
No, poetry itself has become...

21:05.460 --> 21:07.970
I should throw it all away.

21:08.690 --> 21:11.070
Then I will give up poetry.

21:11.790 --> 21:13.260
Only poetry...

21:15.010 --> 21:18.020
Only poetry can set me free...

21:18.400 --> 21:20.950
So please sing for me, Teika.

21:22.280 --> 21:23.350
Noriko-sama...

21:24.030 --> 21:26.400
You are no longer with me...

21:27.840 --> 21:30.970
But if that is your wish...

21:31.900 --> 21:36.170
As I wait for someone
who will never come,

21:36.930 --> 21:38.730
my body burns like the seaweed

21:38.730 --> 21:40.550
drying on the shores of Matsuho.

21:42.200 --> 21:44.310
I wait, but you will never come.

21:44.900 --> 21:49.980
Yet my love for you will
always burn inside me.

21:51.730 --> 21:56.100
I will continue to write poetry,
even after you're gone.

21:57.040 --> 21:59.770
I will pass our poems down.

22:05.200 --> 22:06.810
Thank you, Teika-dono.

22:07.440 --> 22:09.600
These screens look wonderful now.

22:10.030 --> 22:12.770
No, I should thank you.

22:13.190 --> 22:15.310
I've reaffirmed my love of poetry.

22:15.850 --> 22:17.770
When presented with a poem,

22:17.770 --> 22:21.150
I can see the emotions behind it.

22:21.660 --> 22:26.560
People, both now and then,
have always had the same worries.

22:27.240 --> 22:28.350
Yes.

22:29.350 --> 22:31.530
Poems are almost alive.

22:32.230 --> 22:35.250
I wish to pass them
on so they never die.

22:36.520 --> 22:41.250
If future generations are able
to share the feelings they had,

22:41.250 --> 22:44.170
that would be a wonderful thing.

22:42.110 --> 22:44.170
Poetic Tale 13:

22:42.110 --> 22:44.170
END
